  "ingredients": [
    "4 1/2 ounce chicken sausage (such as Artisan Fresh)",
    "5 large egg yolk",
    "1/4 cup coconut flour",
    "1/2 teaspoon dried rosemary",
    "1/4 teaspoon cayenne pepper",
    "1/4 teaspoon baking soda",
    "1/8 teaspoon kosher salt",
    "3/4 cup cheddar cheese (shredded)",
    "1/4 cup coconut oil",
    "2 tablespoon unsweetened carton coconut milk",
    "2 teaspoon lemon juice"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 350F. Cut the cheddar and bacon sausages into cubes. I'm using a brand called Artisan Fresh.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/CSBPIMG_1971-0001.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Separate the yolks from the whites, discarding the whites — unless you'd prefer to save them to make some Peanut Butter Meringue Cookies.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/CSBPIMG_1973-0002.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the sausages to a pan over medium-high heat. Cook until browned, then set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/CSBPIMG_1976-0003.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a mixing bowl, measure out the coconut flour, rosemary, cayenne pepper, baking soda, and salt.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/CSBPIMG_1991-0006.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grate as much cheese as you'll need for the recipe (if you're not the biggest fan of cheese, you can use a bit less than what the recipe states).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/CSBPIMG_2014-0009.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beat the egg yolks until they reach a creamy consistency — this will take about 4–5 minutes. I use only one of the whisk attachments on my hand mixer, since there is not that much liquid.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/CSBPIMG_1984-0004.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the coconut oil, coconut milk, and lemon juice to the egg yolk mixture and beat until smooth creamy.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/CSBPIMG_1990-0005.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slowly fold the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients. Once finished, fold in the grated cheddar.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/CSBPIMG_1997-0007.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide the batter evenly into ramekins, filling them about three-quarters of the way full to leave room for the sausage.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/CSBPIMG_2007-0008.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Submerge the sausages evenly throughout the batter, pushing some pieces down deeper than others to have sausage throughout the pies while leaving some on top for decoration.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/CSBPIMG_2022-0010.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 20–25 minutes. Serve and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-cheese-breakfast-pie/#wprm-recipe-50893-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/BreakfastPie4.jpg"
    }
  ],
